dynamoDB: fully managed highly available with replication across multiple AZs. Doesn't use SQL. Single-digit milisecond and everything is integrated with IAM. 
Standard & Infrequent access/IA table class
dynamoDB:
1) tables with primary key
2) rows
3) each item has an attribute
4) data types supported are: scalar types(string,number,binary,...), document types(list,map), set types(string set,...)
provisioned mode: default saying how much read and write you expect. 
on-demand mode: automatically scales read and write
RCU/ read capacity units: how many times you can read
WCU/Write capacity units: how many times you can write
DyncamoDB Accelerator/DAX: fully-managed,highly available, resolves read congestion by caching
stream processing: orderd stream of item-level in a table
TTL/Time to live: automatically delete items after an expiry timestamp
PITR/Point-in-time recovery: creates a point in time recovery object. 
on-demand backups: full backups for long-term retention






